{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/492418-chicago-workings-and-mummy-geometry","id":492418,"title":"Chicago Workings and Mummy Geometry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-26T01:20:06-07:00","id":492418,"title":"Chicago Workings and Mummy Geometry","content":"So, with the lack of Relic Architecture rules, I've been mucking around and reading up on various interpretations of the concept in other (preferably blue book) sources. And this SAS caught my eye. The opening in particular is rather fascinating. The whole story has a very God-Machine vibe to it, but there's an off-handed mention about an architect embracing ancient Egyptian designs and conflicting with another favouring more modern virtues. And then there are the mechanics of the geometry in the story. It manipulates the emotions of people in the area, and once focussed can provide a number of interesting effects from inflicting illness to creating clone-like proxies or even lifeless slaves. Those powers made me think of Infrastructure, but... there's a certain sense of Vestige-like power in how people live differently according to the geometry shaping their part of the city.<br /> <br /> In a nutshell, it does entertain me to think of the story as a conflict between competing Irem-inspired and God-machine-inspired geometric magic, although neither of the mortals involved would necessarily be aware of their sources. And the descriptions helped me to finally put together a proper write-up for my Tef-Aabhi player on how to go about achieving his own experiments in geometry. The actual story predates both Mummy and the God-Machine Chronicles, but I found many of the ideas inside it were not too dissimilar to how I'd been thinking on the subject.<br /> <br /> Without any mechanics of Relic Architecture out there at the moment, I've not been able to do much with geometry in my games beyond specific examples (in other words, it's effects are facts of the setting specific to particular stories, as opposed to a system the players can interact with on a mechanical level). In that respect, Chicago Workings was pretty helpful in providing more ideas for such stopgap measures. Does anyone know of any similar books along these lines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T04:15:35-07:00","id":492505,"title":"","content":"I wasn't aware of this before, so thanks for mentioning.<br /> <br /> After a quick look, I'd say seeing it as mummy like or god-machine like is the wrong way to think about it. <br /> <br /> Spiritual resonance is just a fact of metaphysics in nwod, the god-machine (probably) just takes advantage of that, and sekhem is a natural force so iremite magic taking advantage of the same thing is a natural, iremite magic always seemed to me to be scientific in nature- cause and effect. <br /> <br /> And since the two geomancers got their magic from the same source, how is one using iremite magic and the other occult matrices? A more natural way to get those involved is to say that a mummy or cult became aware of one, and the god-machine the other, so their being used as unwitting proxies.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if geomancy interests you, sanctum and sigil has rules for ley lines and manipulating the resonance of mana by manipulating the feng shui.<br /> <br /> The ordo dracul practices some geomancy, according to their book, allowing them to gain bonuses to attribute rolls. <br /> <br /> The architects of the monolith, from bloodline the hidden, have a geomantic discipline.<br /> <br /> And second sight has a bit about geomancy in the thaumaturge section if memory serves. <br /> <br /> So vampires, mages, thaumaturges, mummies, and demon/gmc, it's not exactly an exclusive club. <br /> <br /> Considering that mortals can do it, it might even be considered occultism ala the book antagonists. If you don't have antagonists, the idea is that some rituals just work, whether it's the ritual itself, an outside force empowering it, an object of power used in the ritual, whatever, allowing plain mortals to use a little magic ritually. <br /> <br /> Oh and mysterious places has a place that was made a genius locus in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T04:32:11-07:00","id":492507,"title":"","content":"Sorry, Root and Burnham were the two conflicting architects who seemed like they could have been influenced by different sources (see page 2 and its brief mention of &quot;authentic Egyptian designs&quot;), not Ellsworth and Burgess.<br /> <br /> And yes, geometric magic would be something that could be carried out by mortals. They would have to be, since most Arisen aren't active long enough to be building the networks themselves. Thanks for the tips. I knew of the Ordo Dracul and Second Sight's brief mention. Neither of them seemed to be as overtly magical as the Rite of Irem Reborn from Cursed Necropolis D.C. or the magic at play in Chicago Workings, however.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the merit at the back of Chicago Workings, Architectural Attunement, seems like it could easily be used to determine the location of a Mummy's tomb in the nearby area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T23:39:55-07:00","id":493331,"title":"","content":"Ah, get you now.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for the impressiveness of the geomancy in that SAS, if you'll notice, as mortals, the geomancers didn't do anything more impressive than any of the examples I gave you, it wasn't until they died and became ghosts that their geomancy kicked into high gear. Other than their attunement merit, as mortals all they seem to have done is change the feng shui of their area ala the sanctum and sigil rules. <br /> <br /> In second edition, of course, that would just be the ghosts having an anchor- their geomantic workings, which would allow them to influence it.<br /> <br /> In first edition, in which that isn't a thing, it was suggested that ghosts can tap into resonance like a spirit in Bloody Mary's case, so it would be shaping resonance to empower a ghost.<br /> <br /> The phantom caller, a ghost that merged with the phone system, would be a similarly evolved ghost.<br /> <br /> As for being able to sense tombs, I wouldn't say all tombs, but tombs with at least a point in geometry, or the endowments- obscure or radiant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-27-2015, 02:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T23:20:58-07:00","id":494439,"title":"","content":"Hm. True enough, although the implication that they're inflicting serious diseases on one another does go a little bit above the feng shui of Second Sight as I recall.<br /> <br /> Still, it wasn't so much the idea of directly porting the Geometric magic of the SAS into Mummy that had me interested, but rather using it as inspiration for the effects of Iremite Geometry (Tef-Aabhi projects in particular) in the absence of Relic Architecture rules. I'm not one for creating entire rule systems, but since I'm currently running a Chronicle it seemed like good inspiration for the consequences and mechanics of a particular story.<br /> <br /> Thus, the general idea I'm playing with is someone trying to create a Geometric network and Lifeweb that would cross a city and help slow the Descent, much like the effects that currently, uh, &quot;bless&quot; Washington D.C. In order to construct something like that, I figured it would require a network not dissimilar to the one described in the book, consisting of a lot of real estate built across the city according to the correct principles. By tying Vestiges into this enlargened Lifeweb, they could accomplish one of a couple of set effects, depending upon their purposes.<br /> <br /> You're right in that Architectural Attunement shouldn't be able to detect Tombs without a dot of Geometry, but since a tomb is basically a closet with only one dot of Geometry... what even <i>is</i> a no Geometry tomb? Just some floating Peril and a hole in the ground for the khat/canopic jars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T09:06:01-07:00","id":494889,"title":"","content":"Yeah, without geometry or endowments a tomb would just be a place with lots of traps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}